<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Merchant of Venice</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1596–<a href="/years/1598">1598</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Merchant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> is a play by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-shakespeare">William Shakespeare</a>, written in the late 1590s. It tells of the Venetian merchant Antonio, who borrows money from the Jewish moneylender Shylock on the bond of a pound of his flesh, and of Portia, who saves him in court. Its portrayal of Shylock has made it one of Shakespeare's most discussed plays. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a> translated it into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-merchant-of-venice.jpg" alt="The Merchant of Venice" width="320" height="466" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Merchant_venice_tp.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
